{
  "summary": "Resolved the six implementation hazards from the previous critique with concrete, minimal-complexity fixes: (1) use a persistent `override: bool` field on FeatureFile instead of history scanning, set/cleared by _cmd_move_feature; (2) split _dependency_dirty into two flags (_deps_edited_dirty for depends_on mutations, _deps_stage_dirty for terminal transitions only) so the cache rebuild is scoped to events that actually change resolution status; (3) fix the plan_invalidation_check race by having it remove the feature ID from _auto_plan_queued and set a poison flag on the in-flight task's context dict so the planning phase aborts early with a 'dependency invalidated' note rather than producing a stale plan; (4) cap dependency_events at 50 entries with LRU eviction of addressed events only (unaddressed events are never evicted), and have the planning prompt consume only unaddressed events rather than the full list; (5) replace the len(unresolved_deps) heuristic with a proper topological sort using Kahn's algorithm on the dependency subgraph of current impl_stages candidates, falling back to original ordering for features with no dependency relationships to preserve existing behavior; (6) extend resolve_dependencies() return schema to {blocked: bool, unresolved_deps: [ids], dangling_deps: [ids], override: bool} so all four states (unblocked, blocked-by-unresolved, blocked-by-dangling, overridden) are distinguishable by callers without re-running resolution. Additionally identified two new gaps: the dependency_events schema needs exactly four event types (dep_rejected, dep_done, dep_dangling_detected, dep_override_warning) with required fields {ts, event, dep_id} and optional fields {dep_title, note, addressed}, and the _cmd_edit_depends_on handler must validate that proposed dependencies are on the same board before running cycle detection, since cross-board ID collisions (while unlikely with 8-char hex) would produce silent incorrect blocking."
}
